  "id": "psychophysiological-assessment",
  "term": "psychophysiological assessment",
  "definition": "Psychophysiological assessment is the measurement of bodily responses linked to psychological functioning. In this source, it refers specifically to measuring the auditory startle reflex and how quickly it occurs after a loud sound, as a possible indicator of neural processing speed and psychiatric risk or status.",
